  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nConditions overall look to be drier on Sunday, although a few \npassing weak waves may generate some showers earlier in the day. A \nfront will move into the area Sunday evening/night with additional \nshowers/storms possible, with an isolated threat of severe weather \nproviding storms can become organized and survive into our area. \nWith timing of the front arrival later in the day for much of our \narea, not expecting much of a threat for our region particularly \nsouth and east of the Ohio River.\n\nThe weather will turn increasingly warm as we progress into next \nweek as an upper ridge takes hold across the area. Heat indices by \nthe middle of next week should easily climb back into the mid to \nupper 90s. Differences exist towards the end of the week in the \nmodels concerning timing of breakdown of ridge and return of \nunsettled conditions, but increasing chances for showers and storms \nare expected towards the end of the week and into the weekend as a \nfront approaches, and multiple waves move along the front through \nthe area, possibly bringing a return of heavier showers and storms \nback to the area.",
